id: pm-covpax
title: "Successful linked-test receipts carry non-actionable execution_context and all-zero failure_categories, even under --lean"
description: "Found while delivering pm-gh1630. After a selective run's tests[] was bounded to the selected entries, the remaining cost of a successful pm test --run receipt is mostly constant plumbing. On a 1-test --only-last run that passed: default TOON 2198 bytes, --lean 2178, --json 2685, --lean --json 2645. Every variant contains the full execution_context block (about 1.2 KB): requested and actual pm_context_mode, source and sandbox project and global paths, item counts, extension seeding flags, workspace roots and the trust fingerprint. It also contains a 9-row failure_categories map of zeros. When the run passed and mismatch_detected is false, an agent cannot act on any of it.\n\npm-fqdmbf (closed) hoisted the execution context to once per invocation and made --lean drop successful empty streams. Its acceptance criterion 'Lean structured output omits non-actionable successful-run sandbox plumbing while failures retain enough provenance' was delivered for streams only. This item covers the remaining boundary: what a successful, mismatch-free receipt must say about its sandbox, and whether all-zero failure categories need to be printed at all."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 3
tags[3]: agent-ux,linked-tests,token-efficiency
created_at: "2026-10-30T13:12:13.481Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-30T23:44:24.911Z"
closed_at: "2026-10-30T14:06:27.219Z"
completed_at: "2026-10-30T14:06:27.219Z"
author: "harness:claude-code"
estimated_minutes: 120
acceptance_criteria: "Measure the default, lean and JSON receipts for passing and failing runs, with and without a context mismatch; Define which execution_context fields are actionable on success and project the rest behind an explicit restore path, keeping full provenance on failure, refusal or mismatch; Render failure_categories compactly when every count is zero, without losing the counts on failure; Keep CLI, SDK and MCP shapes consistent and record the measured byte reduction"
parent: pm-5t33or
risk: low
confidence: high
severity: low
resolution: "Lean CLI output for a passing, mismatch-free, all-zero-category run projects execution_context to its modes, trust reason and restore_with, and omits zero failure categories. Failures, skips, mismatches and default output keep full provenance."
expected_result: "A passing, mismatch-free linked-test receipt omits non-actionable sandbox plumbing and zero-count categories by default or under --lean, with a documented way to restore them; failures keep full diagnostic provenance."
actual_result: "58-test --only-last passing run: lean TOON 2178 to 865 bytes, lean JSON 2645 to 1166. The failing lean run keeps 21 context fields and non-zero categories. Default output is unchanged. Unit coverage spans success, trust reason, failure, non-zero category, mismatch and skip variants."
component: cli
