comments[2]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-30T13:12:13.481Z","harness:claude-code","Duplicate check: a semantic search for execution_context and linked-test receipt verbosity, and a keyword search for execution_context. Closed pm-fqdmbf is the nearest owner. Its resolution records hoisting plus lean removal of successful streams only, and the live CLI shows execution_context in every variant, so this is a distinct, still-open boundary rather than a recurrence. Measured on this branch (feat/agent-same-command-corrections) in an isolated tracker."
  "2026-10-30T14:06:26.121Z","harness:claude-code","Implementation evidence: the change is CLI presentation only. SDK runTest results and test-all summaries are unchanged. projectLinkedTestEvidence already hoisted the shared context and, under --lean, dropped successful streams. It now also projects a quiet success when lean is set, ok is true, every row passed, the shared context has mismatch_detected false and every failure category is zero. In that case execution_context becomes {pm_context_mode, workspace_context_mode, trust_reason, restore_with: 'rerun without --lean'} and failure_categories is omitted. Any failure, skip, non-zero category, mismatch or heterogeneous context keeps the full 21-field context and the categories. The default and non-lean JSON shapes are unchanged, so existing parsers are unaffected. Measured on the 58-test fleet item, --only-last passing run on this branch: lean TOON 2178 to 865 bytes (-60%), lean JSON 2645 to 1166 bytes (-56%). Default TOON stays 2212 and default JSON 2695. A deliberately failing lean run keeps all 21 context fields with sandbox paths and assertion_failure: 1. A first draft compacted the context on an ok run with a non-zero category; the unit test caught it and the condition now requires all-zero categories. output.spec 41/41, the linked-test trust integration test, test-command and test-all suites, ESLint and the static quality gate (LOC cap; execution.ts shrank) pass."
